From ee1bfe1ba9c39d0b16dcbf1996f0f6e83796557a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:59:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] conn: Only uncount connections that were counted as
 opened

rep_hist_note_conn_opened() is called from listener_connection_new(),
and through note_connection() once an accepted connection has passed
connection_init_accepted_conn() or an outbound connect() has started.
But connection_mark_for_close_internal_() called
rep_hist_note_conn_closed() for every connection, and that counter is
clamped at 0, so every connection closed without having been counted
pulled tor_relay_connections{state="opened"} down towards 0:

  - Accepted OR connections whose TLS handshake fails right away in
    connection_init_accepted_conn(), because the peer had already sent
    non-TLS bytes or closed before we called accept(). This happens a
    lot when the main loop is too busy to accept quickly.
  - Transparent proxy connections rejected in
    connection_init_accepted_conn().
  - Connections without a socket that never go through connect(): the
    linked exit and directory connections of every BEGIN_DIR stream,
    the linked AP and directory connections of tunneled directory
    requests, exit streams closed while resolving, and DNSPort requests.
  - Outbound directory connections whose connect() fails right away.

Also, Extended ORPort connections are counted as such when accepted but
become OR connections in connection_ext_or_transition(), and were then
uncounted as OR connections.

Flag a connection when it is counted, and only uncount flagged
connections, as or_connection_t's tracked_for_dos_mitigation already
does for the DoS subsystem. Move a counted Extended ORPort connection to
the OR counters when it becomes an OR connection.

Fixes #41350
